  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's motion and perception interface, exposing all motion commands as controllable events and all sensor outcomes as uncontrollable events. The specification E1 encodes a conservative exploration and obstacle-avoidance policy: in clear states, the robot alternates between random_walk and short forward progress; upon any obstacle event, it immediately enters a dedicated recovery state with a single turn action, and only resumes exploration after path_clear. The supervisor never enables forward or random_walk in obstacle states, and always processes uncontrollables before controllables, ensuring safety and progress.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant for motion/perception interface, specification for safe exploration policy.",
    "Use helper commit states for one-shot motion actions; obstacle events force immediate recovery with a single turn direction per obstacle."
